												</div>
												{"\n"}
												<p>
													{"We recommend the "}
													<code>
														{"classic"}
													</code>
													{" template so that you can get started quickly, and it contains features found in Docusaurus 1. The "}
													<code>
														{"classic"}
													</code>
													{" template contains "}
													<code>
														{"@docusaurus/preset-classic"}
													</code>
													{" which includes standard documentation, a blog, custom pages, and a CSS framework (with dark mode support). You can get up and running extremely quickly with the classic template and customize things later on when you have gained more familiarity with Docusaurus."}
												</p>
												{"\n"}
												<p>
													{"You can also use the template's TypeScript variant by passing the "}
													<code>
														{"--typescript"}
													</code>
													{" flag. See "}
													<a class="" href="/docs/typescript-support">
														{"TypeScript support"}
													</a>
													{" for more information."}
												</p>
												{"\n"}
