														</pre>
														<div class="buttonGroup_KXnS">
															<button type="button" aria-label="Copy code to clipboard" title="Copy" class="clean-btn">
																<span class="copyButtonIcons_gMWc" aria-hidden="true">
																	<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="copyButtonIcon_GXfb">
																		<path fill="currentColor" d="M19,21H8V7H19M19,5H8A2,2 0 0,0 6,7V21A2,2 0 0,0 8,23H19A2,2 0 0,0 21,21V7A2,2 0 0,0 19,5M16,1H4A2,2 0 0,0 2,3V17H4V3H16V1Z"></path>
																	</svg>
																	<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="copyButtonSuccessIcon_ktUX">
																		<path fill="currentColor" d="M21,7L9,19L3.5,13.5L4.91,12.09L9,16.17L19.59,5.59L21,7Z"></path>
																	</svg>
																</span>
															</button>
														</div>
													</div>
												</div>
												{"\n"}
												<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetHideOnScrollNavbar_qJOx" id="project-structure-rundown">
													{"Project structure rundown"}
													<a href="#project-structure-rundown" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Project structure rundown" title="Direct link to Project structure rundown" translate="no">
														{"​"}
													</a>
												</h3>
												{"\n"}
												<ul>
													{"\n"}
													<li class="">
														<code>
															{"/blog/"}
														</code>
														{" - Contains the blog Markdown files. You can delete the directory if you've disabled the blog plugin, or you can change its name after setting the "}
														<code>
															{"path"}
														</code>
														{" option. More details can be found in the "}
														<a class="" href="/docs/blog">
															{"blog guide"}
														</a>
													</li>
													{"\n"}
													<li class="">
														<code>
															{"/docs/"}
														</code>
														{" - Contains the Markdown files for the docs. Customize the order of the docs sidebar in "}
														<code>
															{"sidebars.js"}
														</code>
														{". You can delete the directory if you've disabled the docs plugin, or you can change its name after setting the "}
														<code>
															{"path"}
														</code>
														{" option. More details can be found in the "}
														<a class="" href="/docs/docs-introduction">
															{"docs guide"}
														</a>
													</li>
													{"\n"}
													<li class="">
														<code>
															{"/src/"}
														</code>
														{" - Non-documentation files like pages or custom React components. You don't have to strictly put your non-documentation files here, but putting them under a centralized directory makes it easier to specify in case you need to do some sort of linting/processing"}
														{"\n"}
														<ul>
															{"\n"}
															<li class="">
																<code>
																	{"/src/pages"}
																</code>
																{" - Any JSX/TSX/MDX file within this directory will be converted into a website page. More details can be found in the "}
																<a class="" href="/docs/creating-pages">
																	{"pages guide"}
																</a>
															</li>
															{"\n"}
														</ul>
														{"\n"}
													</li>
													{"\n"}
													<li class="">
														<code>
															{"/static/"}
														</code>
														{" - Static directory. Any contents inside here will be copied into the root of the final "}
														<code>
															{"build"}
														</code>
														{" directory"}
													</li>
													{"\n"}
													<li class="">
														<code>
															{"/docusaurus.config.js"}
														</code>
														{" - A config file containing the site configuration. This is the equivalent of "}
														<code>
															{"siteConfig.js"}
														</code>
														{" in Docusaurus v1"}
													</li>
													{"\n"}
													<li class="">
														<code>
															{"/package.json"}
														</code>
														{" - A Docusaurus website is a React app. You can install and use any npm packages you like in it"}
													</li>
													{"\n"}
													<li class="">
														<code>
															{"/sidebars.js"}
														</code>
														{" - Used by the documentation to specify the order of documents in the sidebar"}
													</li>
													{"\n"}
												</ul>
												{"\n"}
												<h3 class="anchor anchorTargetHideOnScrollNavbar_qJOx" id="monorepos">
													{"Monorepos"}
													<a href="#monorepos" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Monorepos" title="Direct link to Monorepos" translate="no">
														{"​"}
													</a>
												</h3>
												{"\n"}
												<p>
													{"If you are using Docusaurus for documentation of an existing project, a monorepo may be the solution for you. Monorepos allow you to share dependencies between similar projects. For example, your website may use your local packages to showcase latest features instead of depending on a released version. Then, your contributors can update the docs as they implement features. An example monorepo folder structure is below:"}
												</p>
												{"\n"}
												<div class="language-bash codeBlockContainer_jDV4 theme-code-block" style="--prism-color: #393A34; --prism-background-color: #f6f8fa;">
													<div class="codeBlockContent_cKMj">
														<pre tabindex="0" class="prism-code language-bash codeBlock_Gebt thin-scrollbar" style="color: rgb(57, 58, 52); background-color: rgb(246, 248, 250);">
															<code class="codeBlockLines_FJaf">
																<div class="token-line" style="color: rgb(57, 58, 52);">
																	<span class="token plain">
																		{"my-monorepo"}
																	</span>
																	<br />
																</div>
																<div class="token-line" style="color: rgb(57, 58, 52);">
																	<span class="token plain">
																		{"├── package-a "}
																	</span>
																	<span class="token comment" style="color: rgb(107, 107, 107); font-style: italic;">
																		{"# Another package, your actual project"}
																	</span>
																	<span class="token plain"></span>
																	<br />
																</div>
																<div class="token-line" style="color: rgb(57, 58, 52);">
																	<span class="token plain">
																		{"│   ├── src"}
																	</span>
																	<br />
																</div>
																<div class="token-line" style="color: rgb(57, 58, 52);">
																	<span class="token plain">
																		{"│   └── package.json "}
																	</span>
																	<span class="token comment" style="color: rgb(107, 107, 107); font-style: italic;">
																		{"# Package A's dependencies"}
																	</span>
																	<span class="token plain"></span>
																	<br />
																</div>
																<div class="token-line" style="color: rgb(57, 58, 52);">
																	<span class="token plain">
																		{"├── website   "}
																	</span>
																	<span class="token comment" style="color: rgb(107, 107, 107); font-style: italic;">
																		{"# Docusaurus root"}
																	</span>
																	<span class="token plain"></span>
																	<br />
																</div>
																<div class="token-line" style="color: rgb(57, 58, 52);">
																	<span class="token plain">
																		{"│   ├── docs"}
																	</span>
																	<br />
																</div>
																<div class="token-line" style="color: rgb(57, 58, 52);">
																	<span class="token plain">
																		{"│   ├── src"}
																	</span>
																	<br />
																</div>
																<div class="token-line" style="color: rgb(57, 58, 52);">
																	<span class="token plain">
																		{"│   └── package.json "}
																	</span>
																	<span class="token comment" style="color: rgb(107, 107, 107); font-style: italic;">
																		{"# Docusaurus' dependencies"}
																	</span>
																	<span class="token plain"></span>
																	<br />
																</div>
																<div class="token-line" style="color: rgb(57, 58, 52);">
																	<span class="token plain">
																		{"├── package.json "}
																	</span>
																	<span class="token comment" style="color: rgb(107, 107, 107); font-style: italic;">
																		{"# Monorepo's shared dependencies"}
																	</span>
																	<br />
																</div>
															</code>
														</pre>
														<div class="buttonGroup_KXnS">
															<button type="button" aria-label="Copy code to clipboard" title="Copy" class="clean-btn">
																<span class="copyButtonIcons_gMWc" aria-hidden="true">
																	<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="copyButtonIcon_GXfb">
																		<path fill="currentColor" d="M19,21H8V7H19M19,5H8A2,2 0 0,0 6,7V21A2,2 0 0,0 8,23H19A2,2 0 0,0 21,21V7A2,2 0 0,0 19,5M16,1H4A2,2 0 0,0 2,3V17H4V3H16V1Z"></path>
																	</svg>
																	<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="copyButtonSuccessIcon_ktUX">
																		<path fill="currentColor" d="M21,7L9,19L3.5,13.5L4.91,12.09L9,16.17L19.59,5.59L21,7Z"></path>
																	</svg>
																</span>
															</button>
														</div>
													</div>
												</div>
												{"\n"}
												<p>
													{"In this case, you should run "}
													<code>
														{"npx create-docusaurus"}
													</code>
													{" within the "}
													<code>
														{"./my-monorepo"}
													</code>
													{" folder."}
												</p>
												{"\n"}
												<p>
													{"If you're using a hosting provider such as Netlify or Vercel, you will need to change the "}
													<code>
														{"Base directory"}
													</code>
													{" of the site to where your Docusaurus root is. In this case, that would be "}
													<code>
														{"./website"}
													</code>
													{". Read more about configuring ignore commands in the "}
													<a class="" href="/docs/deployment/netlify">
														{"deployment docs"}
													</a>
													{"."}
												</p>
												{"\n"}
												<p>
													{"Read more about monorepos in the "}
													<a href="https://yarnpkg.com/features/workspaces" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">
														{"Yarn documentation"}
													</a>
													{" (Yarn is not the only way to set up a monorepo, but it's a common solution), or check out "}
													<a href="https://github.com/facebook/docusaurus" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">
														{"Docusaurus"}
													</a>
													{" and "}
													<a href="https://github.com/facebook/jest" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">
														{"Jest"}
													</a>
													{" for some real-world examples."}
												</p>
												{"\n"}
												<h2 class="anchor anchorTargetHideOnScrollNavbar_qJOx" id="running-the-development-server">
													{"Running the development server"}
													<a href="#running-the-development-server" class="hash-link" aria-label="Direct link to Running the development server" title="Direct link to Running the development server" translate="no">
														{"​"}
													</a>
												</h2>
												{"\n"}
												<p>
													{"To preview your changes as you edit the files, you can run a local development server that will serve your website and reflect the latest changes."}
												</p>
												{"\n"}
												<div class="theme-tabs-container tabList_Qoir">
													<ul role="tablist" aria-orientation="horizontal" class="tabs">
														<li role="tab" tabindex="0" aria-selected="true" class="tabs__item tabItem_AQgk tabs__item--active">
															{"npm"}
