													<div class="admonitionContent_Knsx">
														<p>
															<code>
																{"npm install"}
															</code>
															{" may report several vulnerabilities and recommend running "}
															<code>
																{"npm audit"}
															</code>
															{" to address them. Typically, these reported vulnerabilities, such as RegExp DOS vulnerabilities, are harmless and can be safely ignored. Also read this article, which reflects our thinking: "}
															<a href="https://overreacted.io/npm-audit-broken-by-design/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="">
																{"npm audit: Broken by Design"}
															</a>
															{"."}
														</p>
